1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,508
Last time you met the kappa.

2
00:00:01,625 --> 00:00:03,215
But could one actually work?

3
00:00:03,262 --> 00:00:04,794
It's the size of a child,

4
00:00:04,957 --> 00:00:06,722
yet legends say it drags horses

5
00:00:06,722 --> 00:00:07,546
into rivers.

6
00:00:07,709 --> 00:00:08,510
That's a tug of war it

7
00:00:08,510 --> 00:00:09,275
can't win.

8
00:00:09,358 --> 00:00:11,017
So do what a crocodile does.

9
00:00:11,134 --> 00:00:12,156
Grab from the water,

10
00:00:12,156 --> 00:00:13,374
and drag prey in,

11
00:00:13,374 --> 00:00:14,964
where it can't plant its feet.

12
00:00:15,720 --> 00:00:17,240
But drowning takes time,

13
00:00:17,450 --> 00:00:18,842
and a kappa needs air.

14
00:00:19,272 --> 00:00:21,384
So breathe like a softshell turtle,

15
00:00:21,397 --> 00:00:23,137
using its mouth lining and skin.

16
00:00:23,649 --> 00:00:25,008
But a kappa climbs out,

17
00:00:25,008 --> 00:00:26,806
and wet skin dries fast.

18
00:00:27,318 --> 00:00:29,246
So store water like the water-holding

19
00:00:29,246 --> 00:00:29,883
frog,

20
00:00:29,896 --> 00:00:31,648
in its bladder and skin.

21
00:00:32,404 --> 00:00:33,773
But the kappa keeps its water

22
00:00:33,773 --> 00:00:35,026
in a dish on its head.

23
00:00:35,654 --> 00:00:36,721
That's the twist.

24
00:00:36,989 --> 00:00:38,568
A creature built on stored water

25
00:00:38,568 --> 00:00:39,879
can't afford to spill it.

26
00:00:40,391 --> 00:00:41,366
So when you bow,

27
00:00:41,366 --> 00:00:42,538
and it bows back,

28
00:00:42,702 --> 00:00:44,082
it loses everything.

